================================================================================
CHANGE 6 — measure the modal at its displayed size (follow-up report)
================================================================================

Reported with modal-shrink-and-grow.mp4 after Changes 1-5: with flip (and drop),
the modal animated in at one width and snapped about 30px wider when the effect
ended. The nested reset-password layer snapped narrower.

OLD_SECTION
    var dimension = getDimensionOfHidden(source);
    layer.height = dimension["height"];
    layer.width = dimension["width"];

    freezePage(); //no-op for every layer after the first
...
    modalStack.push(layer);
    applyWidths(layer);
    if (layer.dock != null) {

NEW_SECTION
    freezePage(); //no-op for every layer after the first
...
    modalStack.push(layer);
    applyWidths(layer);
    measureLayer(layer);
    if (layer.dock != null) {

plus, before positionLayer():

function measureLayer(layer) {
    var overlay = layer.overlay;
    overlay.style["visibility"] = "hidden";
    overlay.classList.add("show");

    layer.host.innerHTML = layer.source.outerHTML;
    var probe = layer.host.childNodes[0];
    probe.style["display"] = "block";
    probe.style["width"] = "100%";
    var box = probe.getBoundingClientRect();
    layer.width = box.width;
    layer.height = box.height;

    layer.host.innerHTML = "";
    overlay.classList.remove("show");
    overlay.style["visibility"] = "";
}

REASON
getDimensionOfHidden() measured the hidden source as position:absolute, which gives
its shrink-to-fit width: the content's natural width, capped by the viewport. That
has nothing to do with the width from config.modalWidths / data-widths, which is the
width the host shows the modal at. The animation box (effectsCon) used the
shrink-to-fit size and the host used the configured width, so the modal snapped to a
new width when the effect ended. The text then rewrapped and the height changed too.
Content narrower than the configured width grew (the sign-in form). Content wider
than it shrank (the reset-password paragraph runs wider than 500px on one line).

The mismatch is older than Changes 1-5. They make it more visible because the
content no longer blinks at the same moment.

The modal is now measured inside its own host, with the overlay shown but
visibility:hidden, after applyWidths() and before positionLayer(), which reads
layer.height. The probe keeps its id, so id-based styles count in the measurement.
Two copies share the id only for this synchronous block.

