CHANGE 7 — split halves anchored to their outer edge (follow-up report)
================================================================================

Reported with modal-wrong-split.mp4 after Change 6: during split, the halves did
not form the modal. Each half showed the modal's left side ("Sign in" was visible in
both halves).

OLD_SECTION
        fillEffectBox(leftEle, layer)["style"]["left"] = "0px";
        fillEffectBox(rightEle, layer)["style"]["right"] = "0px";
  (and the same two calls with leftE / rightE in closeEffects.split)
...
    source.style["width"] = layer.effect == "split" ? layer.width + "px" : "100%";

NEW_SECTION
        fillSplitHalf(leftEle, layer, "left");
        fillSplitHalf(rightEle, layer, "right");
  (and fillSplitHalf(leftE/rightE, ...) in closeEffects.split)
...
    source.style["width"] = "100%"; //split sizes its copies through fillSplitHalf()'s wrapper

function fillSplitHalf(half, layer, side) {
    var wrap = $$.ce("DIV");
    wrap.setAttribute("style", "position:absolute; top:0; " + side + ":0; width:" + layer.width + "px;");
    half.innerHTML = "";
    half.appendChild(wrap);
    return fillEffectBox(wrap, layer);
}

REASON
Each half is 50% as wide as the modal, with overflow:hidden, and holds a copy of the
whole modal. The copy was in normal flow, so it started at the half's left edge in
both halves, and the right half showed the left side. The left/right:0 the old code
set on each copy was meant to anchor it to its edge. It had no effect because the
copy was never positioned.

The copy now sits in an absolutely positioned wrapper anchored to the half's outer
edge. The wrapper is as wide as the host (layer.width from Change 6), and the copy is
100% of it, the same as in the host. So the halves line up with the displayed modal,
and the copy's width no longer depends on its box-sizing. The source's
split-specific pixel width is no longer needed.

================================================================================
CHANGE 8 — split halves are not autofillable (follow-up report)
================================================================================

Reported after Change 7: the split halves still did not match. The left half's
inputs had a white background and the right half's did not.

OLD_SECTION
function fillSplitHalf(half, layer, side) {
    var wrap = $$.ce("DIV");
    wrap.setAttribute("style", "position:absolute; top:0; " + side + ":0; width:" + layer.width + "px;");
    half.innerHTML = "";
    half.appendChild(wrap);
    return fillEffectBox(wrap, layer);
}

NEW_SECTION
function fillSplitHalf(half, layer, side) {
    var wrap = $$.ce("DIV");
    wrap.setAttribute("style", "position:absolute; top:0; " + side + ":0; width:" + layer.width + "px;");
    wrap.setAttribute("inert", "");
    half.innerHTML = "";
    half.appendChild(wrap);
    var copy = fillEffectBox(wrap, layer);
    var fields = copy.querySelectorAll("input, textarea, select");
    for (var x = 0; x < fields.length; x++) {
        fields[x].setAttribute("readonly", "");
        fields[x].setAttribute("autocomplete", "off");
    }
    return copy;
}

REASON
The white background is the browser's autofill style (:-webkit-autofill), not
library or page CSS. The two halves are two separate copies of the same form, and
Chrome autofilled only one of them (the left one). So one half showed filled,
autofill-coloured fields and the other showed empty, dark ones. Script cannot read
or copy autofill state, so neither copy is left fillable. Autofill skips read-only
fields, and inert keeps the decorative copies unfocusable while they move. The
copies are thrown away at the hand-off, so these attributes never reach the
displayed modal.

Trade-off: for split only, the modal still lands as a copy rebuilt from markup (the
two halves cannot be handed over as one node), so autofill fills the displayed
fields a moment after the effect ends.
